    "evidence_text": "Aluminum fluoride stimulates surface protrusions in cells overexpressing the ARF6 GTPase\n\nUse of synthetic peptides to locate novel integrin alpha2beta1-binding motifs in human collagen III.\n\nEach motif was verified using shorter synthetic peptides.\n\nTwo sequence motifs from HIF-1alpha bind to the DNA-binding site of p53.\n\nThe binding affinity was independent of the hydroxylation state of P564.\n\nOxidative stress contributes to the developmental toxicity of HU.\n\nThe formyl group is coordinated by His-9 and a bound water on the floor of the groove.\n\nHow oncogenic signalling coordinates glycolysis and anabolic biosynthesis in cancer cells remains unclear.\n\nChem.\n\nG6PD release was evaluated by enzyme activity and Western blot analysis.\n\nLastly, there was no basal or PDGF-stimulated phosphorylation of G6PD.\n\nPGAP2 mutations, affecting the GPI-anchor-synthesis pathway, cause hyperphosphatasia with mental retardation syndrome.\n\nThe mutations cosegregated in the investigated families.\n\nTransfection of the altered protein constructs, p.\n\nLeu127Ser, and p.\n\nThus, we conclude that both AlpA and AlpB contribute to H. pylori laminin binding.",
